# Chandam Project - Cursor Rules

You are working on **Chandam (ఛందం)**, a Telugu/Sanskrit/Kannada poetry meter analysis system.
It analyzes poems to identify metrical patterns — 379 Telugu rules, 554 tested examples, 96.09% accuracy.

## Critical Constraints

### DO NOT MODIFY these projects (undocumented domain knowledge):
- `Chandam.Core/` — Matching engine, scoring, pattern recognition
- `Chandam.Rules/` — 343+ rule data classes
- `Chandam.Util/` — Contracts, enums, Manager classes
- `Chandam.Indic/` — Indic script processing
- `Chandam.Samples/` — Sample poem datasets

If you suspect a bug in core logic, report it — don't fix it.

### Preserve Telugu Authenticity
- Never force English translations of Telugu terms
- Maintain full Unicode support in all layers
- Test with actual Telugu text, not transliterated placeholders

### KISS Principle
- No future-proofing or speculative features
- Small, focused functions with mandatory parameters
- Solve the current problem only

## Architecture

```
Core/ (READ-ONLY)
  Chandam.Util       <- no deps (contracts, enums)
  Chandam.Indic      <- Util (script processing)
  Chandam.Rules      <- Util (data classes only)
  Chandam.Samples    <- standalone
  Chandam.Core       <- Util, Indic (business logic)
  Chandam.Dictionary <- standalone (HTTP + disk cache)

API/
  Chandam.API          <- Core, Util, Indic (service layer)
  Chandam.API.WebApi   <- HTTP REST API (8 endpoints)

MCP/
  Chandam.MCP.Tools    <- 7 shared MCP tool definitions
  Chandam.MCP.Stdio    <- MCP server (Claude Desktop)
  Chandam.MCP.Http     <- MCP HTTP/SSE server

Web/
  Chandam.Wasm         <- Blazor WebAssembly app
```

Rules are loaded at **runtime** via JSON/YAML — not compiled in.

## Tech Stack
- C# / .NET 8.0, Blazor WebAssembly, xUnit
- MCP (Model Context Protocol) for AI agent integration
- YAML preferred for Telugu text config (YamlDotNet)
- Docker + docker-compose

## Build & Test
```bash
dotnet build Chandam.sln
dotnet test Chandam.MCP.Tests              # 13 MCP tests
dotnet test Chandam.API.IntegrationTests   # 554 examples
dotnet publish Chandam.Wasm -c Release -p:ExcludeYaml=true  # WASM build
```

## Coding Standards
- N-Layer: Interface -> Service -> Data Access + Contracts
- No business logic in data access
- Constants in constants folder; secrets in `.env`
- Commit format: `[Phase#] Category: Description`

## File Placement
- Docs: `Docs/plans/` (plans), `Docs/execution/` (status)
- Scripts: `Docs/Scripts/` (all .sh, .ps1, .bat)
- Rule configs: `Chandam.Config/Rules/` (JSON/YAML)
- Baselines: `Chandam.Config/Baselines/`

## Domain Terms
- Chandam (ఛందం) = Meter/Prosody
- Padyam (పద్యం) = Poem/Verse
- Gana (గణము) = Metrical foot
- Yati (యతి) = Caesura
- Prasa (ప్రాస) = Rhyme
- Vruttam (వృత్తము) = Meter type

## Known Gotchas
- `-p:ExcludeYaml=true` must be CLI property (not csproj) to propagate globally
- Core projects were net4.8, now net8.0 SDK-style
- HybridGlobalization in WASM reduces ICU data (~400KB saved)
